From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: on the console a DirectDraw game's surfaces aren't lost
 on a deactivation (Wine patch 1043)

Arcanum (#747) stopped drawing at its menu: a deactivation, a click on the desktop around its 800x600 window, lost its surfaces, and it polled IsLost about 18,000 times a second waiting to be activated again. The console has nothing to switch to, so DirectDraw leaves the device as it is there.
---
 ...deactivation-doesn-t-lose-the-device.patch | 50 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1043-ddraw-on-a-ps5-title-a-deactivation-doesn-t-lose-the-device.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1043-ddraw-on-a-ps5-title-a-deactivation-doesn-t-lose-the-device.patch b/wine/patches/1043-ddraw-on-a-ps5-title-a-deactivation-doesn-t-lose-the-device.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..af0b5eb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1043-ddraw-on-a-ps5-title-a-deactivation-doesn-t-lose-the-device.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] ddraw: On a PS5 title, a deactivation doesn't lose the
+ device.
+
+The console shows one program and has nothing to switch to, so a
+deactivation is a click on the desktop around the game's window. Arcanum
+(800x600 on a 1920x1080 desktop) then stopped drawing: its surfaces were
+lost, and it polled IDirectDrawSurface7::IsLost about 18,000 times a
+second without a Restore, waiting to be activated again, while its sound
+and the pointer went on (+ddraw: no update_frontbuffer after the last
+picture, only IsLost).
+
+device_parent_activate now leaves the device as it is on a deactivation
+when WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR is set (the title's Wine starter sets it, as
+kernelbase's init_debugger reads it). Elsewhere nothing changes.
+---
+ dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c b/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
+index 8814c32..04bb532 100644
+--- a/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
++++ b/dlls/ddraw/ddraw.c
+@@ -5046,6 +5046,24 @@ static void CDECL device_parent_activate(struct wined3d_device_parent *device_pa
+ 
+     TRACE("device_parent %p, activate %#x.\n", device_parent, activate);
+ 
++    /* On a PS5 title (its Wine starter sets WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR, as kernelbase's
++     * init_debugger reads it) the console shows one program and has nothing to
++     * switch to, so a deactivation is a click on the desktop around the game's
++     * window (Arcanum's 800x600 on a 1920x1080 desktop). Its surfaces were lost,
++     * and a game that waits for them to come back, polling IsLost and restoring
++     * them only when it is activated again, never drew another picture: there the
++     * device stays as it is. */
++    if (!activate)
++    {
++        static int on_ps5 = -1;
++
++        if (on_ps5 < 0) on_ps5 = GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR", NULL, 0 ) > 0;
++        if (on_ps5)
++        {
++            TRACE("deactivation ignored: the console has no other program to switch to.\n");
++            return;
++        }
++    }
+     if (!activate)
+     {
+         ddraw->device_state = DDRAW_DEVICE_STATE_LOST;
